      "side": 0,
      "message": "Since we are building a Python project, the version of Python we need to use is determined by the build backend (\"scikit-build-core\", in our case). This creates the risk of find_package(Python ...) finding the wrong Python version and creating a broken build. scikit-build-core solves this by setting the Python_EXECUTABLE and Python_INCLUDE_DIR (not DIRS) overrides. Those tell find_package(Python ...) exactly which Python to use. We then pass on those variables (alongside some scikit-build-core-specific variables) to ensure the sub-builds find_package(Python ...) behaves as expected.",
      "parentUuid": "3def0f16_14c406e7",
      "revId": "8846340b2b29a6350bf08a3a3a24f6063becfd9a",
